# Aiur alert definitions, keyed by event-topic glob patterns.
#
# Matching rules (see lib/aiur/events/topic.ex):
#   - `*` matches exactly one topic segment
#   - `#` matches zero or more segments
#   - When multiple patterns match the same topic, the one with the most
#     literal segments wins (specificity sort, descending). Ties broken
#     lexicographically by pattern string.
#
# Authoritative-event-wins:
#   - The `chat.send` entry was dropped in Ticket B (was already removed
#     as noise in orchestrator.ex prior).
#   - `task.merging` was dropped; the merge sound now fires on the
#     GitHub-authoritative `ticket.*.pr.merged` event instead of the
#     orchestrator's `task.*` label-flip path.
#   - `task.done` was dropped; close sound now fires on the
#     GitHub-authoritative `ticket.*.issue.state.changed` event with
#     state: closed.
#   - `task.cancelled` and `task.canceled` were consolidated into a
#     single entry matching `state_reason: :not_planned` on
#     `ticket.*.issue.state.changed`.

